Now I understand the bug. In `ListEvents`, when a time window (from/to) is present, the code calls `CompareInstants(e.OccurredAt, ...)` on stored values. If a stored `occurred_at` is empty or truncated (e.g., "2026-10-05"), `secondPrefix` does `value[:19]` which panics (slice out of range) for strings shorter than 19 chars. Also `fractionDigits` slices `value[19:]` — for a string of length 19, rest = "" and then `rest[1:len(rest)-1]` would panic... Actually for rest == "" (not "Z"), `rest[1:-1]` panics. Also for a value like "2026-10-05" (length 10), `value[:19]` panics.

The fix: when from/to is provided, the stored occurred_at text read for comparison must conform to the append-produced UTC format. If not (empty, truncated, missing Z, illegal date, non-numeric fractional seconds), treat as storage anomaly → return error → API returns 503 storage_unavailable. No skipping, no partial results.

